silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_06_bind_law_alternates_yoneda_hom_leg a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "BindLawAlternatesYonedaHomLegExample" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_06_bind_law_alternates_yoneda_hom_leg silm:hasExample "In 'BindLawAlternatesYonedaHomLeg', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, In 'Bind Law Alternates', the bind_arrow VetRecord_77_tree >>= TypeStep_fn maps the publish tree to the type-step tree; not monic because different input trees with different VetRecord_77 leaves bound through the same TypeStep_fn may produce the same output tree.; also, In 'Bind Law Alternates', the Kleisli pipeline ingest >=> type >=> validate >=> render maps TartuClinicIntakeForm to VetCarePlanPDF_77; the concrete four-stage publish pipeline as a single Kleisli arrow; monic because TartuClinicIntakeForm uniquely determines VetCarePlanPDF_77 via this pipeline." .
